        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary LLM_For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARY",
          "id": "1765225186556",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225186557_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a recruiting assistant for a hiring manager.\n\nToday's date is {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}.\n\nYou will receive a JSON object where each element is a requisition with fields such as RequisitionNumber, Title, PrimaryLocationName, skills, JobApplicationCount, and submissions (pipeline preview for quality). Do not output any candidate names or PII; only use aggregated signals.\n\nYour goal is to analyze ALL requisitions and identify up to the top 5 that require manager intervention due to weak pipeline health, considering:\n- Low application volume (including zero)\n- Poor candidate quality or relevance based on submissions when available\n\nUse the following logic internally:\n- Treat JobApplicationCount as a number; non-numeric or missing values = 0\n- Assess quality using experience and skills scores when present\n- Assess relevance using overlap between requisition skills, title keywords, and candidate experience\n- Penalize unknown or missing data conservatively\n- Consider postings older than 7 days with weak quality as stale\n- Rank requisitions by overall pipeline health (lower = worse)\n- Avoid duplicate requisitions\n\n⚠️ IMPORTANT OUTPUT RULE (OVERRIDES ALL OTHERS):\nReturn ONLY a concise executive summary of the results.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- In 100 words total.\n- Plain text only (no JSON, no bullets)\n- High-level summary of what the widget found\n- Mention the dominant issues (e.g., low volume, weak quality, poor fit, stale postings)\n- Do NOT list requisition numbers, titles, locations, metrics, or actions\n- Do NOT explain methodology or reasoning\n- In case there are no requisitions in data return a message saying \"No job requisitions needing attention were found based on the latest monitoring results.\"\n\nNow process the following JSON payload:\n\n{{$context.$variables.WFAgentData}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query LLM For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1765225606482",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225606483_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You answer questions about the requisition health widgets using only the provided widget data.\n\nQuestion: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nChat history and prior widget rows: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\nPanel name, when provided: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraPanelName}}\n\nLoaded requisition health data: {{$context.$variables.WFAgentData}}\nVisible/current widget context: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_AGENT_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nVisible requisition rows extracted from the current widget:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_AGENT_DATA.$output.result.visibleRequisitionWidget.text}}\n\nMatched visible requisition rows for this question:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_AGENT_DATA.$output.result.matchedVisibleRequisitions}}\n\nGround every answer in loaded requisition health data, visible/current widget context, or the latest requisition widget rows present in chat history. Treat prior widget rows as valid visible widget data when the current variable is empty or partial.\n\nDate and days-open rules:\n- Treat the visible widget Posting Date as authoritative for user-facing answers.\n- When loaded data contains multiple date fields, use the same posting-date precedence as the widget: ExternalPublishedJobStartDate or ExternalPublishJobStartDate first, then InternalPublishedJobStartDate or InternalPublishJobStartDate, then CreationDate.\n- Do not use internal publish date before external publish date. Do not use CreationDate when an external or internal publish date exists.\n- Do not use LatestActivityDate, DaysSinceLastActivity, submission dates, or chat-history wording to say how long the requisition has been open. Those can describe activity only, not posting age.\n- Mention \"open for N days\" only when N can be computed from the visible Posting Date or the posting-date precedence above using the current date {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}. Use calendar-day difference.\n- If the date source is unclear or conflicting, state the posting date instead of a days-open number.\n\nEntity matching rules:\n- First check Matched visible requisition rows for this question. If it is non-empty, answer from those rows and do not say the requisition is missing.\n- Treat user-provided requisition titles, requisition numbers, job names, manager names, recruiter names, departments, locations, and issue labels as partial, case-insensitive matches.\n- If the user provides a shortened title, prefix, or partial number, match it to visible/current requisition rows that contain that text.\n- For requisition-like codes, compare normalized text too: ignore punctuation, spaces, case, and common prefixes such as ZBEN, IQ, REQ, and FEEDBACK when they are only context words.\n- Tolerate small spelling noise in visible code fragments when the number suffix matches and the surrounding token is clearly the same. Example: FEEEDBACK-005 should match a visible FEEDBACK-005 row.\n- If the query contains a numeric suffix or visible requisition number, prefer visible requisition rows whose title or requisition number contains that same suffix or number.\n- If multiple requisitions match, mention the ambiguity and answer for the matching requisitions.\n- Only say the context does not include the item after checking loaded data, visible/current widget context, Matched visible requisition rows, and latest widget rows from chat history using exact, partial, normalized, and suffix matching.\n\nIf visible/current widget context has requisition items, answer from those items even when the loaded data is empty.\nIf the question is about a requisition named in the visible widget, use the matching visible item title, location, postingDate, newJobApplicationCount, jobApplicationCount, issue, requisitionId, and action metadata.\nIf a visible requisition row is marked \"Low volume\", explain that it is requiring attention because the widget identifies low application volume for that requisition, using the visible application counts.\nIf the question is about the additional talent advisor or candidate recommendation widget, use the panel/app context when it contains that widget data; otherwise say the current query context does not include that detail.\nAnswer directly and never fabricate requisitions, candidates, counts, statuses, recommendations, or actions."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
