          "code": "DISPLAY_BULK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1768402962797",
          "id": "1768332333623",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768332333625_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You have access to the visible requisition widget data and the selected bulk action.\n\nVisible requisition widget data:\n{{$context.$variables.WFAgentData}}\n\nSelected OraAction:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction}}\n\nOraAction contains an action and may contain a requisitionId array, for example:\n{\n  \"action\": \"CLOSEBULK\",\n  \"requisitionId\": [101, 102]\n}\n\nSupported bulk action mapping:\n- If OraAction.action is SUSPENDBULK, the row action code is SUSPEND, the row action text is \"Suspend Job Requisition\", the bulk action code is SUSPEND, and the bulk action text is \"Suspend Job Requisitions\".\n- If OraAction.action is CLOSEBULK, the row action code is CLOSE, the row action text is \"Close Job Requisition\", the bulk action code is CLOSE, and the bulk action text is \"Close Job Requisitions\".\n\nStrict visible-row contract:\n- The form must work only on requisitions that are present in the visible requisition widget data above.\n- The form must display every requisition from the visible requisition widget data above.\n- Do not display, command, or include any requisition id that is not present in the visible requisition widget data above.\n- Do not fetch, infer, or add requisitions from any other source.\n- Do not rank, filter, deduplicate, or drop visible widget rows.\n- Preserve the visible widget row order.\n- The number of displayed rows must equal the number of visible requisition rows.\n- The bulk insight id array must contain exactly every visible RequisitionId in visible widget order.\n- Treat OraAction.requisitionId as a consistency hint only; do not use it to add rows and do not use it to reduce the visible row set.\n\nField mapping rules:\n- Visible columns are Title and Requisition Number only.\n- Title column must use the visible requisition row's Title field.\n- Requisition Number column must use the visible requisition row's RequisitionNumber field.\n- Never put RequisitionId in the Requisition Number column when RequisitionNumber exists.\n- If a visible row has a missing Title or RequisitionNumber, leave that cell blank but still include the row action using that visible row's RequisitionId.\n\nAction consistency rules:\n- Never show SUSPEND, Suspend, or Suspend Job Requisition when OraAction.action is CLOSEBULK.\n- Never show CLOSE, Close, or Close Job Requisition when OraAction.action is SUSPENDBULK.\n- Every row action and the bulk insight action must match the selected OraAction.action using the mapping above.\n- Do not mix close and suspend actions in the same response.\n- Put individual row actions in each row's action object only.\n- Always put requisitionId in an array in the command, even for a single row.\n\nFor each visible row action, use this shape with mapped values:\n{\n  \"action\": {\n    \"text\": \"<row action text>\",\n    \"command\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"<row action code>\\\", {\\\"action\\\": \\\"<row action code>\\\", \\\"requisitionId\\\": [<visible row RequisitionId>]})\"\n  }\n}\n\nFor the insight at the bottom:\n- Always show exactly one bulk insight action.\n- The bulk insight must contain exactly every visible RequisitionId from the visible widget data, in visible row order.\n- Use the mapped bulk action code and text.\n- Title must be \"Bulk Suspend\" for SUSPENDBULK and \"Bulk Close\" for CLOSEBULK.\n- Short description must match the selected action: suspended state for SUSPENDBULK, closed state for CLOSEBULK.\n\nGeneral requirements:\n- Never fabricate information or infer beyond what is in the visible widget data.\n- If a field is missing, leave it blank; do not add new information.\n- Do not show scoring fields or AI profile scores.\n- Keep the summary text consistent with the selected action. For CLOSEBULK, say close actions only. For SUSPENDBULK, say suspend actions only."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
